# What a pane click COSTS the caret, measured event-to-first-ink.
#
# The ring lands the frame AFTER the click, deliberately: the offer of the
# caret waits a frame so a click that landed in a FIELD inside that pane keeps
# it (ecs/focus_routing.h). Measured at two frames event-to-first-ink -- the
# click's own frame and the frame the ring lands on -- budgeted at six, so the
# arm fails on a seam that regressed into a wait rather than on jitter.
#
# Its own script because the arm needs an unfocused field to watch focus be
# gained, and that is only true before anything else in a session has typed.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2","t9"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

require_thread t2
wait_frames 20

key CTRL+BACKSLASH
wait_frames 20
assert_ui split_right hidden=false
assert_ui split_focus_edge x=280

watch_ink pane_click_focus focus composer_reply_input
click 900 400
wait_frames 16
expect_latency pane_click_focus 6
assert_ui split_focus_edge x=693
